    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "U.S. Congresswoman Dina Titus joins us. Welcome to Cannabis Economy. I'm your host Seth Adler, download episodes through our App and iTunes, within the iTunes Podcast app, in Google Play, or wherever you currently get your podcasts. First, some supporters to thank, and then U.S. Congresswoman Dina Titus. cannabinoid deep-dive, CBC and CBG, a public service announcement from Steve Hill. Canabicromine or CBC is non-psychoactive like CBD and has been shown to be about 10 times more effective than CBD in treating anxiety and stress. It also displays efficiency in treating inflammation, pain relief, and is both antiviral and anti-tumor. CBC has also been shown to stimulate the growth of bone tissue. Canavidrol or CBG is also non-psychoactive and has been shown to stimulate the growth of new brain cells, including in the elderly. It should be noted that genuinely neurogenic compounds are extremely rare. CBG also stimulates bone growth, is antibacterial, and anti-tumor, and combats insomnia. Go to steepill.com slash can economy for more information. Medmen continues to expand its footprint on the cannabis landscape, opening new stores in Los Angeles, Las Vegas, and the iconic Fifth Avenue in Manhattan. They've also opened a 45,000-foot high-tech cannabis cultivation and manufacturing facility in Nevada. The company has reached a $1 billion valuation, making it the country's first cannabis unicorn, and it's just the beginning. Learn how Medmen is building the future of cannabis today at Medmen.com.",
